acceptance_criteria:
Requirement ids are defined in the description §5 (EARS) and exercised by the §6 behaviour specs.
DONE when, in :inspect (backend) and inspect/ui (npm/Vite/SolidJS frontend), consuming TTD1's (computenet-ocv) reader, RunTimeline, Reconstructor, Fidelity and RunDiffReport without reimplementing any of them:
(1) Journal sources and replay sessions satisfy [TTD2-01]..[TTD2-10], with session listing spawning no host ([TTD2-03]) and expiry releasing the sandbox host ([TTD2-07]);
(2) Timeline addressing and scrubbing satisfy [TTD2-11]..[TTD2-20], reusing TTD1's positions, anchors and advancing cursor ([TTD1-15], [TTD1-17]..[TTD1-19], [TTD1-30], [TTD1-31]);
(3) Fidelity rendering satisfies [TTD2-21]..[TTD2-30], with [TTD2-22] (an UNRECONSTRUCTIBLE cell renders its verdict and reasons and NEVER a value, blank, zero, placeholder or stale value) proven by BS-1 and BS-2 — this is the epic's anchor property and the UI realization of [TTD1-34];
(4) Records-only mode satisfies [TTD2-31]..[TTD2-36], proven by BS-3 — the UI realization of [TTD1-23], the journal-carries-no-topology constraint;
(5) Live-run and compaction interaction satisfies [TTD2-37]..[TTD2-41], proven by BS-4 and BS-5;
(6) Large-journal paging and drag coalescing satisfy [TTD2-42]..[TTD2-47], proven by BS-6;
(7) The run-diff view satisfies [TTD2-48]..[TTD2-54], computing no alignment client-side, proven by BS-7 and BS-8;
(8) Read-only containment satisfies [TTD2-55]..[TTD2-60] — no journal write, no mutation of the inspected graph, no effect fired, no wave/watermark/attention advance, and no graph-write route (that is WKB2's) — proven by BS-11;
(9) Every BS-1..BS-11 scenario exists as a named test: frontend under inspect/ui/test/ and inspect/ui/test/dom/, backend under inspect/src/test/kotlin/civictech/inspect/;
(10) ./gradlew :inspect:test, :timetravel:test, :kernel:test, :concord:test, :demo:agora:test and the repo-wide ./gradlew test are green, and (cd inspect/ui && npm ci && npm run typecheck && npm test) is green — the ui-test required check — with NO new concord corpus scenario, NO CONCORDANCE.md edit, no covers: id claimed for any [TTD2-nn], and no journal-format or WireCodec.VERSION change.

Requirement ids are defined in the description §5 (EARS) and exercised by the §6 behaviour specs.
DONE when, in a new leaf module :timetravel consuming :kernel:
(1) Journal reading satisfies [TTD1-01]..[TTD1-14] — including the read-only and no-host-constructed constraints;
(2) The timeline/position model satisfies [TTD1-15]..[TTD1-19], addressable by record index AND per-source frontier cut;
(3) Offline reconstruction satisfies [TTD1-20]..[TTD1-32], reusing the kernel's own recoverFrom rather than reimplementing replay — with [TTD1-20] proven by BS-3 (reconstruction == live recovery, snapshot-equal for every cell);
(4) The fidelity model satisfies [TTD1-33]..[TTD1-38], with [TTD1-34] (never emit a plausible-but-unverified state; report UNRECONSTRUCTIBLE with reasons and no value) proven by BS-8, and [TTD1-26]/[TTD1-27] (no effect fires during reconstruction) proven by BS-7;
(5) Run diffing satisfies [TTD1-39]..[TTD1-46], including byte-identical JSON reports across repeated runs;
(6) The CLI satisfies [TTD1-47]..[TTD1-53], including the three-way exit code and the no-socket/no-format-change constraints;
(7) Every BS-1..BS-15 scenario exists as a named test under timetravel/src/test/kotlin/civictech/timetravel/;
(8) ./gradlew :timetravel:test, :kernel:test, :concord:test, :demo:agora:test and the repo-wide ./gradlew test are green, with the five kernel durability tests unchanged, no new corpus scenario, no CONCORDANCE.md edit, and no journal-format or WireCodec.VERSION change.
